{"name":"Elise","hex":"#d8d7b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Elise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Hebrew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Elise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Für Elise","blocks":[{"text":"Bagatelle No. 25 in A minor for solo piano, commonly known as \"Für Elise\", is one of Ludwig van Beethoven's most popular compositions. It was not published during his lifetime but discovered by Ludwig Nohl 40 years after his death, and may be termed either a Bagatelle or an Albumblatt. The identity of \"Elise\" is unknown; researchers have suggested Therese Malfatti, Elisabeth Röckel, and Elise Barensfeld."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Beethoven_WoO_59_Erstausgabe.png/330px-Beethoven_WoO_59_Erstausgabe.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F%C3%BCr_Elise"},{"title":"Ken Grimwood","blocks":[{"text":"Kenneth Milton Grimwood was an American author, who also published work under the name of Alan Cochran. In his fantasy fiction, Grimwood combined themes of life-affirmation and hope with metaphysical concepts, themes found in his best-known novel, Replay (1986). It won the 1988 World Fantasy Award for Best Novel."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Ken_Grimwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Grimwood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/Therese_Malfatti_Anonymus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/Therese_Malfatti_Anonymus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Therese Malfatti, widely believed to have been the dedicatee of \"Für Elise\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATherese_Malfatti_Anonymus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Elisabeth_R%C3%B6ckel.jpg/500px-Elisabeth_R%C3%B6ckel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Elisabeth_R%C3%B6ckel.jpg/500px-Elisabeth_R%C3%B6ckel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A portrait of Elisabeth Röckel, by Joseph Willibrord Mähler","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElisabeth_R%C3%B6ckel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Milder_Hummel_Brief.jpg/500px-Milder_Hummel_Brief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Milder_Hummel_Brief.jpg/500px-Milder_Hummel_Brief.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anna Milder-Hauptmann, letter to \"Frau Kapellmeisterin Elise Hummel\", 1830","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMilder_Hummel_Brief.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Ken_Grimwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Ken_Grimwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKenGrim.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9a/Bookgrimwood.jpg/120px-Bookgrimwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9a/Bookgrimwood.jpg/250px-Bookgrimwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9a/Bookgrimwood.jpg/120px-Bookgrimwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con